# Close 6 on a1c with partly ideal inputs: in the open state F's killer P_X is re-armed for the
# close (repeater f removed, P_X retracted, R_X back at (1,5,1), R_Z back at (1,6,1)), S_F made
# sticky (pulls R_F back at c1), and T is teleported into E between c1 and c2 (stands for a T
# returner that places T at c2). Expect: F 0-ticks at c1 (C placed in N1), F's base and R_F land at
# c3 BE, F pushes [T, C] at c4, the door is closed at c6.
design designs/piston-door-3x3/tracks/fast-clean/a1c-107.txt
probe T 1 2 0
probe C 1 1 0
probe E 1 3 0
probe F 1 4 0
probe RF 1 4 -1
probe TL 0 2 0
probe TR 2 2 0
probe M 1 0 0
use 0 4 -2
quiet 24
clear 1 6 -1
clear 1 6 1
quiet 4
clear 0 4 -1
set 0 4 -1 minecraft:sticky_piston[facing=east,extended=true]
quiet 2
clear 1 5 2
set 1 5 1 minecraft:redstone_block
set 1 6 1 minecraft:redstone_block
quiet 4
print
use 0 4 -2
trace 1
clear 2 3 0
set 1 3 0 minecraft:stone
trace 10
